uying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brinker International, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the ownership, development, operation, and franchise of casual dining restaurants in the United States and internationally. It operates and franchises Chili's Grill & Bar and Maggiano's Little Italy restaurant brands. The company was founded in 1975 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin D. Hochman | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $289K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Brinker International, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $7.8B market cap on $5.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $558M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.62\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, 