ave only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $10.0M sold).","It returns 5.7% a year to shareholders (5.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 16.9% of the float, 3.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 20,096 employees, each generates about $289K of revenue, 0.8x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 5.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $28K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.6M (13x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":76,"head":"Watch: composite 55, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $154.","pros":["Composite 55, above the 39 line (gates 16/25)","ROIC 28.6% vs WACC 10.5%","Revenue grew 11.7%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.4x","Piotroski F-score 8/9"],"cons":["Trades 3% above fair value of $181"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":153.81,"vc":{"base":180.95,"base_src":"dcf","bear":119.47,"bull":281.5,"alt_median":118.34,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.5291,"dispersion":0.1284,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 53% above the other models' median ($118)"]},"med":{"pe":17.7245,"ev_ebitda":10.514,"pfcf":15.7535,"pb":2.1712,"roic":0.127,"gross_margin":0.3467,"fcf_margin":0.0625,"div_yield":0.0235}},"mc_quantiles":[81.18,104.73,119.47,127.66,137.46,144.92,153.5,162.04,167.82,173.78,180.81,188.07,197.63,208.54,218.09,228.94,241.15,257.4,281.5,317.74,389.08],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.779,"discount_rate":0.136,"terminal_growth":0.005,"exit_multiple":0.08},"ticker":"EAT","date":"2026-11-20"}